                                        "entry_id": "805fb660-b36e-3912-9179-e0a823146f6b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Shaped as a sphere; being a sphere."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c753405e-0eeb-41e9-8fe8-0acbc63747d5",
                                                "sense_id": "b0248c3b-1bae-3dd3-83bc-0455a36767a8",
                                                "text": "The ability of a segment of a glass sphere to magnify whatever is placed before it was known around the year 1000, when the spherical segment was called a reading stone, essentially what today we might term a frameless magnifying glass or plain glass paperweight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b3a6b7e-69bc-3f61-be34-60d1d33c43f4",
                                        "entry_id": "805fb660-b36e-3912-9179-e0a823146f6b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, or pertaining to, spheres."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "734f1840-dc8e-33db-961c-c15f5b2855f7",
                                        "entry_id": "805fb660-b36e-3912-9179-e0a823146f6b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a coordinate system, specifying the location of a point in a plane by using a radius and two angles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b14539c-0291-361b-a63e-f5455ea018c4",
                                        "entry_id": "805fb660-b36e-3912-9179-e0a823146f6b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to the heavenly orbs, or to the sphere or spheres in which, according to ancient astronomy and astrology, they were set."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72d68e0c-ba1a-4a8a-9def-660e29bd56b3",
                                                "sense_id": "5b14539c-0291-361b-a63e-f5455ea018c4",
                                                "text": "Knaves, thieves, and treachers by spherical predominance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea11773e-a285-3897-aa2a-745d2231b9e5",
